 * 2. Assign a thread tag to the created thread by creating a thread tag assignment (with valid thread_id, assigned_at).
 * 3. Retrieve the thread tag assignment by its id and check all properties (id, thread_id, assigned_at, removed_at) match the previously created assignment.
 * 4. Try fetching a thread tag assignment using a random, non-existent UUID for id, and validate that a not found error is returned.
 */
